  "title": "Reputation Tags",
  "html": "<p>Tags are lasting traits. They describe how society sees a PC, and they amplify (or hamper) specific skills in specific scenes. They are not used up when they come into play.</p>\n<h3>Anatomy of a tag</h3>\n<p>Every tag has four parts:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Word:</strong> the label society uses (&quot;Silver-tongued&quot;, &quot;Hot-headed&quot;).</li>\n<li><strong>Skill:</strong> one skill the tag affects (Persuasion, Insight, Intimidation, Arcana, Performance and so on).</li>\n<li><strong>Scene:</strong> the kind of situation where it matters (at court, in the markets, among temple folk, on the battlefield, in the wilds, in the underworld).</li>\n<li><strong>Pips:</strong> 1 to 3. Pips show how deeply the reputation is set. A new tag starts with 1.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>Examples</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Positive: <strong>Silver-tongued</strong> (Persuasion, at court), 1 pip.</li>\n<li>Positive: <strong>Battle-tested</strong> (Intimidation, on the battlefield), 2 pips.</li>\n<li>Negative: <strong>Hot-headed</strong> (Deception, in negotiations), 1 pip.</li>\n<li>Negative: <strong>Oathbreaker</strong> (Persuasion, among temple folk), 2 pips.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The DM approves the Skill and Scene pairing so that tags stay specific.</p>\n<h3>Positive tags: Amplify</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>When the tag&#39;s scene is in play and you make a check with its skill, you may invoke the tag to gain <strong>advantage</strong> on that check.</li>\n<li><strong>Uses per session</strong> equal the tag&#39;s pips (they refresh at the start of each session).</li>\n<li><strong>At 3 pips (Signature):</strong> once per session, treat a d20 roll below 10 as a 10 on a check the tag covers.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Negative tags: Weigh</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>When the tag&#39;s scene is in play and the skill comes up, the DM or any other player may invoke the tag against you, giving you <strong>disadvantage</strong> on that check.</li>\n<li>It can be invoked against you up to its pips in times per session.</li>\n<li><strong>Each time it is invoked against you, you gain 1 Inspiration.</strong> You can also volunteer to play into it for the same reward.</li>\n<li>You can&#39;t invoke your own negative tags to hurt yourself in order to farm Inspiration beyond that limit.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Earning and deepening tags</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>When:</strong> at each milestone checkpoint, each PC may earn <strong>one</strong> new tag or add <strong>one</strong> pip to an existing tag.</li>\n<li><strong>Criteria:</strong><ul>\n<li><strong>Positive</strong> if you acted in service of duty or morality at a cost to your own desire, or kept to society&#39;s conventions despite real hardship.</li>\n<li><strong>Negative</strong> if you acted on your desire at the cost of duty or morality, or broke society&#39;s conventions.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>You can earn one of each in the same checkpoint.</li>\n<li>If you already have a tag that fits, deepen it instead of making a new one (max 3 pips).</li>\n<li>The group helps choose the Word, Skill and Scene, based on what actually happened.</li>\n<li><strong>Cap:</strong> 3 positive and 3 negative tags at once. At the cap, you must deepen a tag or replace one.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Shedding tags</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Positive tags</strong> can be lost if you act against them in a major way (the DM and player agree), or swapped at an Act Break.</li>\n<li><strong>Negative tags</strong> are removed by in-fiction redemption: an atonement scene, a public apology, a quest or a favour. The DM and player agree when it is done. Removing a negative tag also reduces its pips, one at a time.</li>\n<li>Society remembers. The DM should reflect tags in how NPCs treat the PC.</li>\n</ul>\n"
