  "html": "<p>Fifteen levels is long, so the campaign runs in four acts that follow 5e&#39;s tiers. Each act ends with an <strong>Act Break</strong>: a longer checkpoint that refreshes the Good Society layer before it goes stale.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Act</th>\n<th>Levels</th>\n<th>Scale of play</th>\n<th>Typical stakes</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>I</td>\n<td>5-8</td>\n<td>Local: a few Houses, one region</td>\n<td>Inheritance, marriages, feuds, the first threat</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>II</td>\n<td>9-12</td>\n<td>The capital and the great Houses of Corvane</td>\n<td>Alliances, succession, treaties, a secret that threatens the realm</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>III</td>\n<td>13-16</td>\n<td>The realm and neighbouring powers</td>\n<td>War, a crisis in the ward-network, rival realms</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>IV</td>\n<td>17-20</td>\n<td>The world and beyond</td>\n<td>Planar threats, remaking the Concord, final reckonings</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Pace:</strong> with milestone levelling, plan for about 2-3 sessions per level, so roughly 30-45 sessions in total. Adjust to your group&#39;s schedule.</p>\n<p><strong>Act Break (end of Acts I, II and III), about 20-30 minutes:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Run a normal milestone checkpoint.</li>\n<li><strong>Desires:</strong> each player must either replace their desire or deepen it with a new twist. The old one is marked achieved, abandoned or failed.</li>\n<li><strong>Reputation:</strong> each player may rewrite or swap one tag (new Word, Skill or Scene), and may move one pip from one tag to another. Society&#39;s opinion shifts as the scale of play grows.</li>\n<li><strong>Rumour board:</strong> clear it and start fresh.</li>\n<li><strong>NPCs:</strong> each player may change one NPC&#39;s fortune, retire one NPC and create a replacement, or reset its Leverage to 2.</li>\n<li><strong>Inner conflict:</strong> resolve it if it is mostly full, or reset it.</li>\n<li><strong>PC succession (optional):</strong> a player may retire their PC and bring in a new one at the same level. The old PC becomes an NPC they still control, as in the base game.</li>\n<li><strong>Investment check:</strong> ask everyone if they still want to continue, as Good Society recommends. Reaching an Act Break is a good point to finish if the group is tired.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Final session (level 20):</strong> skip the rumour board. Each player closes with an <strong>epilogue letter</strong> written by their PC, set years after the last scene, describing what became of them and their NPCs. Then title the story together.</p>\n"
